          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em
              super
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theoretical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretical
            version of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+superalgebra"} geometry of physics – superalgebra
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            literature the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal dual
            of super
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            came to be known as “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FDA"}> FDA
            ”s (see remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfintiyAsFDA"}
            below), a decade before plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            were discussed in the mathematical literature. The key example in this context are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            obtained by iterated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+higher+central+extension"} universal higher central extension
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cohomology
            of these (called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tau-cohomology"}> tau-cohomology
            ” in the physics literature) turns out to classify
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            and serves as a tool for the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theories in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p Abstractly, the definition is immediate:
          #SuperLInfinityAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                super
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              (i.e. in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes+of+super+vector+spaces"} chain complexes of super vector spaces
          %p Explicitly this equivalently comes down to the following definition in components:
          #SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (super graded signature of a permutation)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              = succeed "-bigraded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{v} = (v_1, v_2, \cdots, v_n)
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
              of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of homogeneous degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_i, s_i) \in \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V_{(n_i,s_i)}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\vert \sigma \vert}
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature of the permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^k
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is the composite of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              permutations that each exchange precisely one pair of neighboring elements.
            %p
              We say that the
              %em
                super
                = succeed "-graded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{v}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(\sigma, v_1, \cdots, v_n) \;\in\; \{-1,+1\}
            %p
              is the product of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature of the permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\vert \sigma \vert}
              with a factor of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-1)^{n_i n_j}(-1)^{s_i s_j}
            %p
              for each interchange of neighbours
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\cdots v_i,v_j, \cdots )
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\cdots v_j,v_i, \cdots )
              involved in the decomposition of the permuation as a sequence of swapping neighbour pairs (see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              for discussion of this combination of super-grading and homological grading).
          %p
            Now def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityAlgebra"}
            is equivalent to the following def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#L-infinity-algebra#DefinitionViaHigherBrackets"} L-infinity algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            now given by def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
          #sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An
              %em
                super
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+map"} multilinear map
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      \-ary bracket
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi 𝔤
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext copies
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        l_n(\cdots)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        [-,-, \cdots, -]_n
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\underset{n \; \text{copies}}{\underbrace{\mathfrak{g} \otimes \cdots \otimes \mathfrak{g}}}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathfrak{g}
                %p
                  and of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-2
            %p such that the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %strong> super graded skew symmetry
                  ) each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_n
                  is graded antisymmetric, in that for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  elements and for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1, \cdots, v_n)
                  of homogeneously graded elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in \mathfrak{g}_{\vert v_i \vert}
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        l_n(v_{\sigma(1)}, v_{\sigma(2)},\cdots ,v_{\sigma(n)})
                        \=
                        \\chi(\sigma,v_1,\cdots, v_n) \cdot l_n(v_1, v_2, \cdots v_n)
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\sigma,v_1,\cdots, v_n)
                  is the super
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1,\cdots,v_n)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %strong>
                    strong homotopy
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
                  ) for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} (n+1)-tuples
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1, \cdots, v_{n+1})
                  of homogeneously graded elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in \mathfrak{g}_{\vert v_i \vert}
                  the followig
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
                  holds
                #eq:LInfinityJacobiIdentity.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℕ
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo +
                                %mi j
                                %mo =
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi UnShuff
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi l
                            %mi i
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\sum_{{i,j \in \mathbb{N}} \atop {i+j = n+1}}
                        \\sum_{\sigma \in UnShuff(i,j)}
                        \\chi(\sigma,v_1, \cdots, v_{n})
                        (-1)^{i(j-1)}
                        l_{j} \left(
                        l_i \left( v_{\sigma(1)}, \cdots, v_{\sigma(i)} \right),
                        v_{\sigma(i+1)} , \cdots , v_{\sigma(n)}
                        \\right)
                        \= 0
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where the inner sum runs over all
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unshuffles"} unshuffles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  and where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
                  is the super graded signature sign from def.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
            %p
              A
              %em
                strict
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi is
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    is
                    \\mathfrak{g}_1 \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}_2
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
              that preserves the bidegree and all the brackets, in an evident sens.
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism+of+L-infinity+algebras"} strong homotopy homomorphism
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sh+map"}> sh map
              ”) of super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal duals
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCEAlgebra"}
          %p
            In order to define the correct homomorphisms between super
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cohomology
          #SuperLInfinityCEAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A super
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              if the underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              is degreewise of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is of finite type, then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebra"} differential graded-commutative superalgebra
              whose underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
              is the super-Grassmann algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^{\ast}
            %p
              of the graded degreewise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              which on generators is the sum of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+linear+maps"} dual linear maps
              of the
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{g}}
                    \\coloneqq
                    [-]^\ast + [-,-]^\ast + [-,-,-]^\ast + \cdots
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\wedge^1 \mathfrak{g}^\ast
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^\ast
            %p
              and extended to all of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              as a super-graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              of degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
            %p
              Notice that here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              are such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_i \in \mathfrak{g}^\ast_{(n_i,s_i)}
              elements of homogenous bidegree, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha_1 \wedge \alpha_2
                    \\;=\;
                    \-(-1)^{n_1 n_2} (-)^{s_1 s_2}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{g}}
                    (\alpha_1 \wedge \alpha_2)
                    \\;=\;
                    (d_{\mathfrak{g}} \alpha_1) \wedge \alpha_2
                    +
                    (-1)^{n_1} \alpha_1 \wedge (d_{\mathfrak{g}} \alpha_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              (see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              for more on this).
            %p
              A
              %em strong homotopy homomorphism
              (“sh-map”) between super
              = succeed "-algbras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; \mathfrak{g}_1 \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}_2
            %p
              is defined to be a homomorphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
              between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
              going the other way:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{g}_1) \longleftarrow CE(\mathfrak{g}_2)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    f^\ast
            %p
              (here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              is the primitive concept, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is defined as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal dual
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi dgcsAlg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    s L_\infty Alg \hookrightarrow dgcsAlg^{op}
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebras"} differential graded-commutative superalgebras
              on those that are CE-algebras as above.
            %p
              Finally, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              of a super
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              algebra of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              is its
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cohomology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^\bullet(\mathfrak{g}, \mathbb{R})
                    \\;=\;
                    H^\bullet(CE(\mathfrak{g}))
                    \\,.
          #LInfinityTerminology.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Special cases of the general concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
              def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
              go by special names:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in even
              = succeed "-degree," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            %p
              If the only possibly non-vanishing brackets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              are the unary one
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-]
              (which induces the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              on
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is equivalently a (super-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"}> dg-Lie algebra
              \.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in
              = succeed "-degrees" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              then it is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebra
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in degree 0, then it is equivalently a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %p
              Combining this, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in even
              = succeed "-degree" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "-degree" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebra"} Lie n-algebra
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in
              = succeed "-degree" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "-degree," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          %h2#history History
          #SuperLInfintiyAsFDA.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (history of the concept of (super-)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                algebras)
            %p
              The identification of the concept of (super-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              \-algebras has a non-linear history:
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              in the incarnation of higher brackets satisfying a higher Jacobi identity,
            %p
              def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
              and remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityTerminology"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra#LadaStasheff92"} Lada-Stasheff 92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
              that was found in the construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string+field+theory"} closed string field theory
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "string+field+theory#Zwiebach93"} Zwiebach 92
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#L-infinity-algebra#Stasheff16"} Stasheff 16
            %p
              The observation that these systems of higher brackets are fully characterized by their Chevalley-Eilenberg dg-(co-)algebras (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCEAlgebra"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra#LadaMarkl94"} Lada-Markl 94
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiberStasheff08"} Sati-Schreiber-Stasheff 08, around def. 13
            %p
              But in this dual incarnation,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              and more generally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
              (of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature already in
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFreRegge80"} D’Auria-Fré-Regge 80
              and explicitly in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Nieuwenhuizen82"} van Nieuwenhuizen 82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
              (
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
              ) and eventually came to be referred to as “FDA”s (short for “free differential algebra”) in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature (but beware that these dg-algebras are in general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              only as graded-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"}> supercommutative superalgebras
              , not as differential algebras) The relation between super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature is made explicit in (
              %a{:href => "#FSS15"}> FSS 15
              ).
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebra
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                    “FDA”
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              The construction in
              %a{:href => "#Nieuwenhuizen82"} van Nieuwenhuizen 82
              in turn was motivated by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebras"} Sullivan algebras
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "#rational+homotopy+theory#Sullivan77"}> Sullivan 77
              ). Indeed, their dual incarnations in rational homotopy theory are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "#rational+homotopy+theory#Quillen69"}> Quillen 69
              ), hence a special case of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityTerminology"}
            %p
              This close relation between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
              might have remained less of a secret had it not been for the focus of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+minimal+models"} Sullivan minimal models
              on the non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              case, which excludes the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
              from the picture. But the Quillen model of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              effectively says that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+space"} rational topological space
              then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
              is reflected, infinitesimally, by an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+construction"} Sullivan construction
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              was concretely identified as higher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Lie+integration#Henriques"} Henriques 08
              = succeed "-theoretic" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              manifest is in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "rational+homotopy+theory#BuijsFelixMurillo12"} Buijs-Félix-Murillo 12, section 2
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              Every super
              = succeed "-Lie" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} super ∞-groupoid
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth super ∞-groupoid
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              for more on this.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            the
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
          %p
            and its super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            \-extensions to the
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/m2brane"}> m2brane
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity+Lie+2-algebra"} type II supergravity Lie 2-algebra
          %p
            play a central role. Their exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} infinity-Lie algebra cohomology
            governs the consistent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            for super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"}> branes
            \. (See the discusson of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Green-Schwarz+action+functional#BraneScan"} brane scan
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
            for more on this.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            might form a super
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+function"} n-point function
            of the string, in analogy to what happens for the bosonic string in Zwiebach’s
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes+of+super+vector+spaces"} model structure on chain complexes of super vector spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+differential+graded-commutative+superalgebras"} model structure on differential graded-commutative superalgebras
          %h2#References References
          %p
            In their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal dual
            incarnations as super-graded commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            (super
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            had secretly been introduced in
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFreRegge80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tullio+Regge"} Tullio Regge
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Graded Lie algebra, cohomology and supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/156191"} spire
            %li#Nieuwenhuizen82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+van+Nieuwenhuizen"}> Peter van Nieuwenhuizen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Free Graded Differential Superalgebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Istanbul 1982, Proceedings, Group Theoretical Methods In Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/182644/"} spire
          %p
            and hence a whole decade before the explicit appearance of plain (non-super)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "L-infinity-algebra#LadaStasheff92"} Lada-Stasheff 92
          %p
            The concept was picked up in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFre82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf", :title => "Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup"} Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravityErrata.pdf", :title => "errata"} errata
          %p
            and eventually came to be referred to as “FDA”s (short for “free differential algebra”) in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            literature (where in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            one says “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"}> semifree dga
            ”, since these dg-algebras are crucially not required to be free as
            %em differential
            algebras).
          %p
            The relation between super
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            literature is made explicit in:
          %ul
            %li#FSS15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                %strong 12
                02 (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"}> arXiv:1308.5264
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/S0219887815500188"} doi:10.1142/S0219887815500188
            %li#FSS18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/T-Duality+from+super+Lie+n-algebra+cocycles+for+super+p-branes"} T-Duality from super Lie n-algebra cocycles for super p-branes
                %strong 22
                5 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.06536"}> arXiv:1611.06536
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2018.v22.n5.a3"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2018.v22.n5.a3
            %li#FSS18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+rational+higher+structure+of+M-theory"} The rational higher structure of M-theory
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em
                    Proceedings of the
                    %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/"} LMS-EPSRC Durham Symposium
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
                %strong 67
                8-9 (2019) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02834"}> arXiv:1903.02834
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201910017"} doi:10.1002/prop.201910017
          %p also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
